About Us &nbsp;

SharkNinja&nbsp;is a global product design and technology company, with a diversified portfolio of 5-star rated lifestyle solutions that positively&nbsp;impact&nbsp;people’s lives in homes around the world. Powered by two trusted, global brands, Shark and Ninja , the company has a proven&nbsp;track record&nbsp;of bringing disruptive innovation to market and developing one consumer product after another has allowed&nbsp;SharkNinja&nbsp;to enter multiple product categories, driving significant growth and market share gains. Headquartered in Needham, Massachusetts with more than&nbsp;4,100&nbsp;associates, the company’s products are sold at key retailers, online and offline, and through distributors around the world.&nbsp;

AI at SharkNinja

At SharkNinja, we’re building an AI-native culture. We’re not waiting for the future; we’re creating it. Our people are expected to experiment boldly, adopt new tools, and continuously raise what’s possible to create meaningful impact for our consumers. If you believe the best way to do your job hasn’t been invented yet, you’ll fit right in.

Senior&nbsp;Director,&nbsp;Strategic&nbsp;Growth Initiatives &amp; Transformation &nbsp;

London (Battersea Power Station) / Hybrid - frequent domestic and international travel&nbsp

The Role&nbsp;&nbsp;

We have an opportunity for a Principal Engineer in our AI &amp; Algorithms department,&nbsp;working&nbsp;with a particular focus on our defence and security clients.&nbsp;You’ll&nbsp;join a team of talented engineers and scientists designing,&nbsp;building&nbsp;and testing intelligent systems that&nbsp;require&nbsp;cutting edge&nbsp;algorithms.

As&nbsp;one of the senior technical voices in the team,&nbsp;you’ll&nbsp;be&nbsp;architecting the &nbsp; algorithmic&nbsp;approach on&nbsp;our projects, setting the technical bar for others, and helping shape the work we&nbsp;deliver.&nbsp;As well as&nbsp;hands-on engineering,&nbsp;you’ll&nbsp;spend time with clients, using your&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;to win new projects as well as deliver them.&nbsp;You’ll&nbsp;work&nbsp;in multidisciplinary teams that use&nbsp;our labs and computing resources&nbsp;to enable us to deliver&nbsp;ambitious&nbsp;projects.

Much of our defence and security work requires&nbsp;security clearance, so we ask for it up front. You&nbsp;won’t&nbsp;work exclusively in that sector, but a genuine interest in it matters to us.&nbsp;

We&nbsp;offer a flexible approach to hybrid working, although some of the projects you will be working on will require&nbsp;full-time working in the office.

What&nbsp;you’ll&nbsp;be doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Applying data-driven software development in machine learning/AI, applied statistics, and sensor processing, alongside mathematical computing techniques such as digital signal processing, simulation, and numerical optimisation.&nbsp;

